    syllabus_objectives: 'Candidates should be able to master the fundamental principles of Farm Animals In West Africa in line with the official syllabus.',
    updated_at: 'JAMB • WAEC Official Syllabus',
    content: `<p>The breeds of <strong>cattle, sheep, horses, swine,</strong> and other farm animals are important to the agricultural industry in the African region.</p>
<p>This lesson focuses on the <strong>species, breeds, distribution, and uses</strong> of major farm animals in West Africa.</p>
<h2>1. Cattle</h2>
<p><strong>Species:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>Bos taurus</em> (European cattle)</li>
<li><em>Bos indicus</em> (Zebu cattle)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Breeds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>West African Shorthorn</li>
<li>Sokoto Gudali</li>
<li>N'Dama</li>
<li>N'Dama-Sokoto</li>
<li>Sanga</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Distribution:</strong>
Found throughout West Africa.</p>
<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Milk production</li>
<li>Meat production</li>
<li>Draft power</li>
</ul>
<h2>2. Sheep</h2>
<p><strong>Breeds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>West African Dwarf</li>
<li>Djallonké</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Distribution:</strong>
Found in various countries across West Africa.</p>
<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Meat production</li>
<li>Wool production</li>
</ul>
<h2>3. Goats</h2>
<p><strong>Breeds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>West African Dwarf</li>
<li>Sahelian</li>
<li>Red Sokoto</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Distribution:</strong>
Found in various countries across West Africa.</p>
<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Meat production</li>
<li>Milk production</li>
<li>Fibre production</li>
</ul>
<h2>4. Pigs</h2>
<p><strong>Breeds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Large White</li>
<li>Landrace</li>
<li>Duroc</li>
<li>Hampshire</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Distribution:</strong>
Found in various countries across West Africa.</p>
<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Meat production</li>
</ul>
<h2>5. Rabbits</h2>
<p><strong>Breeds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>New Zealand White</li>
<li>Californian</li>
<li>Chinchilla</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Distribution:</strong>
Raised in smaller numbers in urban and rural areas.</p>
<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Meat production</li>
<li>Fur production</li>
<li>Pet keeping</li>
</ul>
<h2>6. Poultry (Chickens)</h2>
<p><strong>Breeds:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Local indigenous breeds</li>
<li>Exotic breeds, such as Rhode Island Red and White Leghorn</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Distribution:</strong>
Found throughout West Africa.</p>
<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Meat production</li>
<li>Egg production</li>
</ul>`
