    syllabus_objectives: 'Candidates should be able to master the fundamental principles of Animals by External Features in line with the official syllabus.',
    updated_at: 'JAMB • WAEC Official Syllabus',
    content: `<p>Animal External parts are any part on the outside of it. Such as tails, legs, claws, skin and beaks. Animals use these parts to help them survive and move about.</p><p><strong>Cattle</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc"><li>Large size, sturdy body structure.</li><li>Long horns (in some breeds).</li><li>Four legs with hooves.</li><li>Hair or fur covering the body.</li></ul><p><strong>Sheep</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc"><li>Medium-sized body.</li><li>Covered in wool or hair.</li><li>Two pairs of limbs with hooves.</li><li>Curved horns (in some breeds).</li></ul><p><strong>Goats</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc"><li>Variable body sizes (small to medium).</li><li>Covered in hair or fur.</li><li>Two pairs of limbs with hooves.</li><li>Curved or straight horns (in some breeds).</li></ul><p><strong>Pigs</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc"><li>Medium to large-sized body.</li><li>Hair or bristles covering the body.</li><li>Four limbs with hooves.</li><li>Straight or curly tail.</li></ul><p><strong>Rabbits</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc"><li>Small to medium-sized body.</li><li>Soft fur covering the body.</li><li>Four limbs with claws.</li><li>Long ears and a short tail.</li></ul><p><strong>Poultry (chickens)</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc"><li>Small to medium-sized body.</li><li>Feathers covering the body.</li><li>Two wings and two legs with claws.</li><li>Beak and comb on the head.</li></ul>`
